From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:10:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] wsi/x11: sw present via MIT-SHM AttachFd, pace sw FIFO

Software X11 present (no DRI3, the launcher's X server or Termux:X11) sent
each frame through the X socket with PutImage, and FIFO was not paced:
the server completes at once and has no real vblank.

- If the server has MIT-SHM >= 1.2, back each swapchain image with a memfd
  segment passed with xcb_shm_attach_fd (Android has no SysV shm), copy
  the frame into it once and send ShmPutImage. Damage rects are clipped
  and copied per rect. Any probe or attach failure keeps the PutImage path
  for the whole chain. MESA_VK_WSI_DEBUG=noshm turns it off.
  The memfd gets F_SEAL_SHRINK | F_SEAL_GROW before AttachFd so the
  server's mapping cannot be SIGBUSed by a shrink (seal failure ignored).
  The per-present GetGeometry is sent after the ShmPutImage on this path,
  so its reply proves the server read the segment before the next copy.
- FIFO / FIFO_RELAXED on the sw path wait on the present thread until the
  next refresh deadline from MESA_VK_X11_SW_REFRESH_HZ (the launcher sets
  the display's max refresh rate). Unset or 0 = unpaced, as before.
  MAILBOX / IMMEDIATE unchanged; present id / vkWaitForPresentKHR (084) and
  the present-thread fence wait (106) unchanged.

Purpose: cheaper sw X11 present, real FIFO cadence; biblioklept
Tested GPU: none for this patch (G615 unavailable); host Xwayland check of the same request path, see worklogs/driver-remaining/117-x11-shm-present.md
Tested Kbase UAPI: n/a
Mesa base range: 5a07217f034b (26.3.0-devel)
Dependencies: csf-v11/083, csf-v11/084, csf-v11/106
Validation test: tests/x11-shm/x11_shm_present_test.c under headless Xwayland: ShmPutImage(attach_fd) 2253-2532 fps vs PutImage 936-998 fps at 1280x720, 445-475 vs 281-301 at 1920x1080 (GetGeometry round trip per frame), readback ok; -extension MIT-SHM falls back to PutImage, readback ok

Generated-by: LLM
